<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="eyebrow">Seven repositories</div>
		<h1>Contribute</h1>
		<p class="lede">Everything is public: the patches, the recipes, the scripts that
		build and publish, and the write-up behind each decision.</p>
		<div class="grid">
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/utsugi-pmaports">
				<div class="n">utsugi-pmaports</div>
				<p>The packages, the 78 kernel patches, the device metapackages, and the
				build and publish scripts.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/poconav">
				<div class="n">poconav</div>
				<p>Car navigation with neural-network voice.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/screenglaze">
				<div class="n">screenglaze</div>
				<p>Screenshots with volume-down + power.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/keepalive">
				<div class="n">keepalive</div>
				<p>Apps that minimise instead of closing.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/app-usage">
				<div class="n">app-usage</div>
				<p>Battery use per application.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/smart-unlock">
				<div class="n">smart-unlock</div>
				<p>Skip the PIN when it is safe to.</p></a>
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/lost-phone">
				<div class="n">lost-phone</div>
				<p>Find the phone without Google.</p></a>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>01</span><h2>Building it</h2></div>
		<div class="sh">
			<div class="bar"><i></i><span>ON YOUR PC</span></div>
			<pre>git clone https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/utsugi-pmaports
cd utsugi-pmaports
scripts/setup-workdir   <b># own pmbootstrap work dir, pinned pmaports, a signing key</b>
scripts/build --all     <b># the kernel takes minutes</b>
scripts/lint            <b># fork bookkeeping and version bumps</b>
scripts/check-upstream  <b># says when a fork has fallen behind</b>
scripts/publish --push  <b># sign and publish</b></pre>
		</div>
		<h3>Two rules that will bite otherwise</h3>
		<div class="grid quiet">
			<div>
				<div class="t">Always bump</div>
				<p>pmbootstrap skips a build whose <code>pkgver-pkgrel</code> already exists
				in any index it knows, and reports success. A forgotten bump looks like a
				publish that changed nothing. Use <code>scripts/bump &lt;pkg&gt;</code>.</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<div class="t">Never move a tag</div>
				<p>Re-tagging the same version leaves the old tarball in the distfile cache
				under the same name, and the build silently uses it.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>02</span><h2>Where help would land</h2></div>
		<div class="scroll">
		<table>
			<tr><th>Area</th><th>What is needed</th></tr>
			<tr><td>Fingerprint</td><td>Four routes are documented as dead ends. A fifth
			would be genuinely new ground.</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Echo on calls</td><td>The canceller is wired and tunable at runtime. It
			needs patience and a second phone.</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Vayu modem</td><td>The fault is pinned to one firmware assertion, and
			everything measured is written down. Nobody has got past it.</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Upstreaming</td><td>Several fixes are not device-specific: the GPS engine
			lock affects every Qualcomm device on postmarketOS, and the dialpad fix belongs
			in KDE.</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Stereo audio</td><td>Would need <code>TERT_MI2S_RX</code> transmitting
			two channels. Kernel work, not configuration.</td></tr>
		</table>
		</div>
		<h3>How the patches are written</h3>
		<p>Each one carries its own explanation above the diff: what broke, what was
		measured, what was ruled out and why the change is what it is. That prose is the
		point &mdash; a patch whose reasoning is lost has to be rediscovered the next time
		it looks wrong. If you send one, write it the same way.</p>
